  "title": "what happens to a choice a worker made on its own, under the recommended option",
  "source": "plan-proposal",
  "source_detail": "implementation-view Q3, option (b)",
  "explanation": "Under option (b), a worker's choice becomes its own small box wired to the part it affected, and [your ruling](#ruling) is the only step that involves you. Nothing waits on you: a choice you never rule on counts as fine. A struck one comes back as a follow-up task before [the end of the run](#end). Options (a) and (c) aren't drawn. (a) stops at the new box, and (c) stops the whole run at a strike.",
